[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi. In looking at the Verso documentation, I didn't see any mention of support for Tables. Is that something that is being considered?</p>",
        "id": 583102186,
        "sender_full_name": "Richard L Ford",
        "timestamp": 1775066320
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I see that some tables can be obtained using math mode. For example:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">$$`</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">\\</span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"bp\">\\</span><span class=\"n\">arraystretch</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"mf\">1.5</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"bp\">\\</span><span class=\"n\">begin</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">array</span><span class=\"o\">}{</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">\\\\</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">\\</span><span class=\"n\">hline</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">\\\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"bp\">\\</span><span class=\"n\">hdashline</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">\\</span><span class=\"kn\">end</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">array</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">`</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>as documented at <a href=\"https://katex.org/docs/supported\">https://katex.org/docs/supported</a>.</p>",
        "id": 583371239,
        "sender_full_name": "Richard L Ford",
        "timestamp": 1775169861
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The built-in Verso markup language doesn't include tables, largely because I haven't yet found a design that's satisfactory (that is, one that allows tables to contain things like bulleted lists, have row headers in addition to column headers, and for a cell to span columns or rows). So for now, genres that support tables do so by providing a suitable directive.</p>\n<p>In the manual genre, the table directive takes a bulleted list of bulleted lists, with the outer bullets being rows and the inner bullets being columns. <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/reference-manual/blob/a9f571737c3e10d6823aa0c80f9ba21045e784ae/Manual/BuildTools/Lake/CLI.lean#L148-L164\">Here's an example</a>.</p>\n<p>But this is definitely a topic that we're continuing to talk about the right approach for.</p>",
        "id": 584151143,
        "sender_full_name": "David Thrane Christiansen",
        "timestamp": 1775633395
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for the information. The verso manual, as far as I can see, does not document all the directives, at least not the table directive. I will study the verso source code further.</p>",
        "id": 584207097,
        "sender_full_name": "Richard L Ford",
        "timestamp": 1775649636
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That one should be documented for sure. Thank you!</p>",
        "id": 584297520,
        "sender_full_name": "David Thrane Christiansen",
        "timestamp": 1775675709
